  {
    "op": "replace",
    "path": "/contentPages/0",
    "raw": "While being on the land, a lot of major changes in Skathian scientific process came to pass. With a wealth of new resources to explore and new states to test it in, the first golden age of the Skath began. The first radiotransmitters bred untold of excitement. We were social creatures, after all, and someone new to talk to was thrilling as a concept.",
    "value": "在陆居期间，海鳞族的科学进程经历了诸多重大变革。随着大量新资源的发现与新环境的开拓，海鳞族迎来了首个黄金时代。首批无线电发射机的问世激起了难以言表的兴奋，我们终究是社会性生物，“能与新对象交谈”这一概念本身就令人心潮澎湃。"
  },
  {
    "op": "replace",
    "path": "/contentPages/1",
    "raw": "Eventually, there was a split in our peoples ideologies: one wanted to embrace The Message and reach to the stars. The others wanted to be left alone, to leave the stars a mystery. While there was no war, there as certainly a schism of sorts. The latter group broke with tradition and the Council and left.",
    "value": "然而，民众的意识形态最终出现了分裂：一方渴望接纳“星间讯息”，向群星进发；另一方则希望独善其身，将星空永留为谜。虽未爆发战争，但确乎出现了某种决裂。后者背离传统，脱离议会，毅然离去。"
  },
  {
    "op": "replace",
    "path": "/contentPages/2",
    "raw": "With our technology advancing,they were able to build cities deeper in Norkumsgath's oceans than ever before. Content in isolation, these Skath disappeared and then...vanished from memory. It was not until the First Contact War over a century later that they were seen again.",
    "value": "凭借技术的进步，他们得以在诺库姆斯加斯的深海中建造前所未有的城邦。甘于孤寂的这群海鳞族逐渐消失，继而...从集体记忆中淡去。直至一个多世纪后的第一次接触战争爆发，他们才再度现身。"
  }
]